adjudication.rationale:
In the newly added API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook authentication check compares the provided header value to `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` using `!==`:

```ts
if (
  req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
  process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
) {
  return res.status(403).json({ message: "Invalid webhook secret" });
}
```

A normal string inequality comparison is not constant-time, so it can theoretically leak information via timing differences during comparison. Using `crypto.timingSafeEqual` (with proper Buffer conversion and length check) is the standard mitigation for secret comparisons. This issue is directly present in the diff.
